msgid "What Cost & Profit Tracking does"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cost & Profit Tracking shows where money was earned or spent: by department, project, customer, region or anything else your company tracks. You put a tracking value, such as a project or a department, on a line of a document."
msgstr ""

msgid "A company can use up to two independent tracking categories, for example Project and Department. Each posted line can carry one value of each category, or none."
msgstr ""

msgid "The value travels with the line from the document through approval and posting into the General Ledger, and the figures here are read from the posted ledger."
msgstr ""

msgid "Posted history is never edited. A mistake is corrected by a linked, approved journal, not by changing the value on a posted line."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every page here is a view of posted figures in the company currency. Revenue is credit-positive, costs are debit-positive and result is revenue minus costs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Getting Started in three steps"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Getting Started page walks a new company through the three steps and says, for each one, whether it is done, what is missing and who can do it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Say what you want to track: give each tracking category a name such as Project or Cost center, so everyone reads the same words (a user with Company Setup rights does this on the Tracking Categories page)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create your first value: enter a name, a start date and, where it applies, a date it is needed by (a user with Tracking entry rights does this on New Tracking Value)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Code an expense and see where it went: on an expense, payment or journal line choose the tracking value, then open the Cost & Profit Explorer to see the amount and the document it came from."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open one of the two examples on the Getting Started page first if you want to see the result before you start."
msgstr ""

msgid "The examples use made-up numbers. They are not your company data and nothing is saved."
msgstr ""

msgid "If no category is switched on for new entries, the steps say so; history already recorded stays readable."
msgstr ""

msgid "What changed in this release"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dimensions is now called Cost & Profit Tracking. Every page, permission and report is the same; only the names changed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Old name and new name: Dimensions menu: Cost & Profit Tracking; Financial Tracking Home: Overview; Financial Tracking Guide: User Guide; Financial Tracking: Cost & Profit Explorer; Dimension Entry: New Tracking Value; Outstanding Dimensions: Open Tracking Values; Dimension Inquiry: Find Tracking Values; Dimension Exceptions: Missing or Invalid Tracking; Dimension Hierarchy: Tracking Hierarchy; Dimension Reports: Cost & Profit Reports; Dimension Summary: Tracking Summary; Dimension Comparison and Exceptions: Tracking Comparison and Exceptions; Dimension Tags: Tracking Tags; Dimension Category Policy: Tracking Categories; Dimension Allocation Journal and Drivers: Cost Allocation Journal and Drivers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Forms, views and reports show your company's own name for each tracking category, for example Department or Project. Until a name is set on the Tracking Categories page, the categories are called Tracking category 1 and Tracking category 2."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each page keeps its place in the menus, and its help link opens the same help page as before."
msgstr ""

msgid "The web address of each page changed with its new name. Old bookmarks still open the right page when the application runs on an Apache web server."
msgstr ""

msgid "Nothing was converted or moved: posted history, budgets, reports, permissions, approvals and saved filters are unchanged."
msgstr ""

msgid "Revenue, costs and result of a tracking value for the period you choose and for its lifetime, with the documents behind each figure."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose the period with From and To, then a value of one or both tracking categories, and press Show. Leave both on their all choice (for example Project: all) to see everything."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tick Unassigned only to list the postings that carry no value of that category."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the result by tracking value first, then the coverage by source family, the budget comparison and the drilldown by account."
msgstr ""

msgid "Coverage tells you how much of the eligible amount carries a tracking value. When coverage is incomplete, the figures describe only the classified part."
msgstr ""

msgid "The net balance of balance-sheet accounts is separate from revenue, costs and result and is not profit."
msgstr ""

msgid "The drilldown lists a limited number of accounts; narrow the scope to see the rest."
msgstr ""

msgid "You need the Tracking view area and GL analytical reports and inquiries. Without the second you see an explicit denial and no amount."
msgstr ""

msgid "Revenue, matched cost, direct contribution, margin and share by customer, with what could not be attributed to a customer listed beside it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose the period and the tracking values as on the Cost & Profit Explorer, then press Show."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read each customer row with its status, then the table of what is not attributed to a customer and the next step for each reason."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the attribution queue to find the source documents that still wait for a customer."
msgstr ""

